  return { root, rig, boardGroup, update(...), setBeakOpen(v), gull(), parts... };
}
```
Wait: the deck's top is at about y=+0.085 (board thickness 0.17 total? Let me set: sphere scaled y by 0.085 → the total thickness = 0.17, so the deck's top is at y = +0.085, plus the rocker bend adds up to ±0.1 near the ends. At the feet position (x=±0.45), the bend is: bend(t) = -0.09*t² + 0.10*((|t|-0.45)/0.55)² where t = x/0.42. For x=0.45, t=1.07 → the bend = -0.09*1.15 + 0.10*(0.62/0.55)² = -0.103+0.127 = +0.024. So the deck rises near the ends. The foot at x=0.45 → the deck top ≈ 0.085+0.024 = 0.109. Set rig.position.y = 0.105 and the feet at y=0.0 relative to the rig → soles at 0.105. Close enough.

Now the pelican body is built in the rig's local coords with the feet at y=0.

